      "problem": "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{12}⁡(23)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's calculate ${log}_{12}⁡(23)$ by changing the base $12$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=12,$ $X=23,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{12}⁡(23) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(23)}{{log}_{10}⁡(12)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(23)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(12)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1.361\\,728}{1.079\\,181} \\\\  & ≈1.262\\end{aligned}\n$$",
